            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 61-year-old male, admitted on 12/04/2022 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed marked rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis with elevated CRP. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. A CT scan of the abdomen was subsequently performed, confirming appendiceal inflammation without perforation. The patient underwent laparoscopic appendectomy uneventfully on 13/04/2022. Postoperatively, he received intravenous fluids, analgesia, and antibiotic therapy. Wound care was performed daily. Recovery was uncomplicated, and the patient was mobilized with physiotherapy support. He was discharged home on 16/04/2022 in good general condition. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>"
            },
